WEBVTT

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:18.640
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.030
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:45.980
And takes me

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.950
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.070
To the home of wind

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.450
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.920
What's wrong, Anne?
Aren't you feeling well?

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:54.590
Oh, Marilla. I'm going to play with Diana
today, so I feel satisfied enough.

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:58.520
But you have to wash
the dishes before that.

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:00.190
Well, eat up quickly.

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:03.590
I wonder what kind of song is
'Nelly in the Hazel Dell'?

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:07.190
Oh! I'm sure Diana's voice is very sweet!

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:08.770
Don't you think Matthew?

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:12.340
Well now, yes.

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:13.080
Anne!

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:18.710
If you continue disobeying me, I shall
cancel your appointment with Diana.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.220
What kind of place is Mrs. Bell's forest?

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:38.890
It must be a nice place.

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:44.240
Because we'll be buildind a playhouse there.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:46.900
Anne!

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:53.290
If you don't finish your
work soon, you will be late.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.380
Didn't you want to look
for some broken china?

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:25.600
Diana, what are you doing?

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:28.270
Nothing, I'm just tidying things up.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.230
Can we play together?
please!

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:37.800
We can't. I'll be going to Green Gables,
so I can't play with you today.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.990
No. I'm going too.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:43.280
But you're going with mother to
the market, aren't you?

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:46.850
No, I want to play with you.

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:48.690
You can't. Now give me that.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:50.420
No, I won't.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:12.180
This can still be used.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:14.050
Matthew!

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:18.370
Can I use this cloth sack?

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:23.950
Well now, I don't mind.
But that cloth sack is kind of old.

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:25.450
Thank you, Matthew!

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:39.630
Snow Queen, I'm going to play with Diana!

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:47.160
Goodness. This child is really strange.

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:31.890
What happened?

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:35.590
I don't believe a best friend would
forget about our appointment.

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:54.220
I'm really not going anywhere.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:57.530
Liar. You said you were going out to play.

00:05:57.530 --> 00:05:58.520
It's true.

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:02.240
What's wrong?

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:05.580
You can't play with me today.
Isn't that right, Anne?

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:11.560
Oh, right! I can't go!

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:14.990
Then goodbye. We'll meet another time, Anne.

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:16.850
Wait for me at the forest.

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:20.440
It's a pity I can't go today.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:24.800
Goodbye, little one.

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:29.260
Anne isn't free today,
we'd better go home, Minnie May.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:55.380
I'm sorry for being late, Anne!

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:06.040
My sister is always like this, but it
doesn't matter now. Let's go!

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:12.270
Diana you liar! You are going to play.

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:16.720
Diana you lied! I want to go too!

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:18.170
What should we do?

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:20.990
How troublesome.

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:26.650
It can't be helped. Bring her along.

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:28.630
I'm sorry. But...

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:32.720
Don't worry, I'm good with children.

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:37.670
I've taken care of three
pair of twins before.

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:41.300
My! I've never heard of anyone who
had three pairs of twins before!

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:45.290
I'm sorry, Minnie May. Don't cry anymore.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:47.840
We'll go play together.

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:51.700
Well, let's go.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:59.290
Minnie May, we're going to go now.

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:01.950
Hurry up!

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:04.820
Mother is calling you. You're not going?

00:08:04.820 --> 00:08:07.230
No, I'm going to play with you.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:11.450
You're not coming with me, Minnie?

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:15.210
Then, I'm going off now.

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:20.420
If you go to Bright River,
maybe you'll get a present.

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:21.430
Really?

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:22.490
Really.

00:08:22.670 --> 00:08:23.760
Really?

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:26.220
Yes, probably.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:30.630
Then we'll play another time.

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:31.580
All right!

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:33.840
Wait!

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:34.370
Let's go.

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:34.460
Wait!

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:35.380
Yes.

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:14.580
What is that?

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:15.930
I don't know.

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:20.430
Wait. Maybe the dwarves live there.

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:23.710
It must be the diamonds
of the dwarves sparkling.

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:26.340
Do you want to see the dwarves?

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:27.910
Yes.

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:37.110
Oh, the light disappeared!

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:45.040
It's just a fragment of a lamp.

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:50.020
No. It's the mirror of sprites.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:54.540
It must be formed with small rainbows.

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:58.110
Is as lovely as a dream.

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:01.520
Diana, look into it.

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:08.380
One night, the sprites
came here for a party.

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:12.020
It was a bustling gathering.

00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:16.530
The sprites forgot the
time while they played.

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:23.940
When the  cock crowed,
they hid desperately.

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:27.060
And they forgot to take this mirror.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:30.790
Lets call it the Mirror of Sprites.

00:10:31.220 --> 00:10:37.840
If we put it in our living room,
every night the sprites would come peep.

00:10:39.770 --> 00:10:41.670
You're really an interesting one.

00:10:46.530 --> 00:10:48.860
Look, we're finally here.

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:58.930
It's here. Do you like it?

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:03.630
It's wonderfull!
Like a small green-roofed house.

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:28.710
Oh, Diana! This is wonderfull.

00:11:28.890 --> 00:11:30.670
It's a very beautiful house.

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:34.270
Isn't it? This is a house
with many Columns.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.400
I was thinking exactly the same.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:40.500
And that would be a lamp of crystal.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:46.970
Because it's got a tremendous glow.

00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:49.600
Diana, thank you for bringing
me to this beautiful house.

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:52.100
I'm very happy too.

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:17.280
Hey!
Do you want to call this the Idlewild?

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:19.300
Idlewild...

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:21.590
It's a very nice name.

00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:24.040
It's very romantic.

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:27.860
How did you come up with such a name?

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:30.520
I didn't think of it just now.

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:35.170
I started thinking of it when
you mentioned this place.

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:40.550
I suddenly thought of the name Idlewild,
when I was doing the dishes today.

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:42.900
I even broke a dish because of it.

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:45.890
Let's begin designing the room.

00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:23.560
Madam, welcome. Please come in.

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:24.950
I shall abide then.

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:34.440
Please take a seat.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:37.420
It looks like a strong couch.

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:40.660
How could you. You should
imagine that it's a soft couch.

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:41.690
I'm sorry.

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:43.750
I'll go prepare tea.

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:49.270
Is your family well?

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:52.350
Yes, madam. Everyone is alright.

00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:55.030
Your living room is really pretty.

00:13:55.650 --> 00:13:57.310
Thank you very much.

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:16.870
What's this?
Did you brought them?

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:22.360
This is the chocolate prince
Matthew brought for me.

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:25.000
We shall split them.

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:28.610
No. We can't forget your sister.

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:29.600
You don't need.

00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:32.990
I do. She cried a big deal over us.

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:35.220
This is yours.

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:37.770
You sister can have two.

00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:40.010
But then you...

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:43.840
I already ate when
I got them yesterday.

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:46.290
And we must be fair in distribution.

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:50.440
Anne Shirley! You are a kind person indeed.

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:53.400
When I got them yesterday,

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:57.300
I thought they would taste much
better if I shared with you.

00:14:58.190 --> 00:15:02.420
Until now I always received things,
but I never had nothing to give.

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:05.080
Well, eat up.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:08.300
No! Please help yourself.

00:15:09.650 --> 00:15:10.880
Thank you, Anne.

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:30.030
It's delicious. It's the first time I
eat such a delicious chocolate.

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:34.000
Not just double, it's triple,
even four times as delicious.

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:05.300
This is so funny.
The world has become rose coloured.

00:16:07.550 --> 00:16:08.710
Hey, Diana...

00:16:09.630 --> 00:16:13.040
I read the book you lent me last night.

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:16.190
It was nerve-wracking from the beginning.

00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:18.860
I felt sorry for the girl.

00:16:18.860 --> 00:16:22.880
Although she has five lovers,
she's not happy at all.

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:24.350
I cried while reading.

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:27.130
She fainted very often, didn't she?

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:29.930
Fainting seems to be so romantic!

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:33.220
Diana, have you ever fainted before?

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:36.180
I want to, but I think it's impossible.

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:39.680
Because skinny people are healthy.

00:16:39.690 --> 00:16:41.510
But I can always act.

00:16:41.940 --> 00:16:42.600
Look.

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:52.400
Are you alright, Anne?

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:54.020
Yes, more or less.

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:57.330
I didn't know fainting was so painful.

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:01.150
I'm going to try too.

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:07.900
How sly!

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:40.090
I became thirsty after laughing heartly.

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:41.260
Me too.

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:42.770
Shall we go to the spring?

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:44.860
You know about that spring?

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:48.230
In the last days I have been
exploring around here.

00:17:48.230 --> 00:17:51.280
And I found that spring.

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:58.060
It's unimaginable. That water flows to
the surface of the earth from below.

00:17:58.060 --> 00:17:59.670
That's right. It's a great spring.

00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:00.490
Let's go!

00:18:12.010 --> 00:18:12.930
It's a rabbit!

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:17.660
That rabbit was wearing clothes.

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:23.200
Right. And had a pocket watch.

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:28.890
Oh dear! Oh dear! I shall be late!

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:30.610
And then it jumped into the the hole.

00:18:30.990 --> 00:18:36.830
Falling all the way
down, down, down, down, down.

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:41.670
You've already read
Alice's Adventures in Wonderland?

00:18:42.690 --> 00:18:44.330
I only read the first chapter.

00:18:44.570 --> 00:18:48.010
Although I wanted to continue,
the candle was burning short.

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:17.860
It's cold.

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:26.110
It's delicious.

00:20:00.820 --> 00:20:04.640
Shall we call this lake, the Dryad's Bubble?

00:20:05.390 --> 00:20:06.850
Dryad's Bubble?

00:20:07.360 --> 00:20:10.920
A Dryad is a tree nymph, isn't it?

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:16.550
That's beautiful.
You're great at giving names.

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:53.200
There was a big bee flying to
a flower just now.

00:20:54.570 --> 00:20:59.520
How happy she must be.
She can live in a flower.

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:04.420
And when the wind shakes her
house, she swings happily.

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:09.260
If I weren't a human being,

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:12.610
I would like to be a bee
and live in a flower.

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:15.920
You are such an imaginative girl.

00:21:18.700 --> 00:21:20.980
I heard about your hat.

00:21:21.200 --> 00:21:24.820
You rigged it with fresh flowers
on the way to Sunday School.

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:29.920
I shouldn't have done it.

00:21:30.400 --> 00:21:32.940
I got scolded by Marilla after that.

00:21:32.940 --> 00:21:38.550
But I don't think putting fresh flowers
on the hat is anything strange.

00:21:38.550 --> 00:21:42.000
Although I've decided to
be good friends with you,

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:46.020
I also hoped to have more friends.

00:21:46.020 --> 00:21:48.360
A pity nobody wanted to talk to me.

00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:51.570
It could be because of the hat.

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:53.740
It must be unrelated to the hat.

00:21:53.740 --> 00:21:58.370
Although I didn't see it.
But Teri said it was pretty.

00:21:58.370 --> 00:21:59.370
Really?

00:21:59.370 --> 00:22:02.410
Yes, although it's something novel,

00:22:02.410 --> 00:22:05.320
but she even wanted to try it.

00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:10.670
I didn't notice that someone though that.

00:22:10.670 --> 00:22:14.360
I think nobody greeted you because

00:22:14.360 --> 00:22:17.130
they didn't know you and
had heard the rumours.

00:22:17.800 --> 00:22:19.730
But things will change for the better,

00:22:20.080 --> 00:22:22.530
because I'll introduce you to everyone.

00:22:26.480 --> 00:22:27.660
Diana!

00:22:28.590 --> 00:22:33.120
I only had imagined friends in the past.

00:22:33.140 --> 00:22:35.070
Katie Maurice was one of them.

00:22:35.080 --> 00:22:37.040
And when I lived in the mountains,

00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:42.070
I imagined that the echo
was a girl called Violetta

00:22:42.630 --> 00:22:44.720
who talked with me.

00:22:45.970 --> 00:22:50.790
But Katie and Violetta are
friends from the past now.

00:22:51.100 --> 00:22:55.040
Because I already have Diana as my friend.

00:23:01.040 --> 00:23:05.190
I'll teach you 'Nelly in the Hazel Dell' now.

00:23:05.380 --> 00:23:06.400
Don't forget it.

00:23:07.500 --> 00:23:08.370
Show me.

00:23:46.130 --> 00:23:47.540
Then we'll meet again tomorrow.

00:23:47.550 --> 00:23:48.970
In the Idlewild, right?

00:23:48.970 --> 00:23:50.580
Yes, I'll be there.

00:23:50.890 --> 00:23:51.950
Then, goodbye.

00:23:52.810 --> 00:23:54.500
Say hello to Minnie May.

00:23:54.500 --> 00:23:55.950
Thank you, Anne!

00:24:16.370 --> 00:24:20.270
Marilla thought Anne lost her
precious amethyst brooch

00:24:20.270 --> 00:24:21.800
and wanted her to confess.

00:24:21.980 --> 00:24:24.950
Next of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:25.220 --> 00:24:27.680
Marilla's Amethyst Brooch Disappears

00:24:27.680 --> 00:24:28.950
Please watch!
